<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct cocoa bean imports up 2.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct cocoa bean imports up 2.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's cocoa bean imports in October totalled 3,481 tonnes, up by 2.5 percent from a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Thursday. The breakdown is as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Oct 96	     Sept 96	 Oct 95</p>
<p> Total		3,481	   5,382	  3,395</p>
<p>Major suppliers (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Ghana		1,802	   3,660	  2,464</p>
<p> Venezuela	    100	     397	    196</p>
<p> Ecuador		603	     286	    177</p>
<p>Cumulative cocoa bean imports in the first 10 months of calendar 1996 were 46,410 tonnes, against 38,316 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Imports of other cocoa products were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 Oct 96	 Sept 96	Oct 95</p>
<p> Cocoa paste	  173		67	     144</p>
<p> Defatted paste	54	     nil	     nil</p>
<p> Cocoa butter     1,775	   1,003	   1,029</p>
<p> Cocoa powder     1,060	     806	     615</p>
<p>Chocolate</p>
<p> confectionery    2,654	   2,022	   2,326</p>
</text>
